#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The nanoHPC Slack agent: answers @-mentions in one Slack channel, runs changes and pushes after an Approve.

Two parts, in one file:

- `nanohpc-agent runner --config RUNNER_JSON`: runs as root on the front node and is the only part that runs
  commands. It listens on a Unix socket that only the agent's account can reach, runs a command only if the rule
  allows it (read-only for anyone; a change only for an approver or after an approver's click), on the front node
  or as root over SSH on another machine, masks secrets in the output, and logs every request. It also keeps its
  own clone of the cluster.yml repository (code changes, pushed after an approver's click) and runs deploys.
- `nanohpc-agent bot --config BOT_JSON`: runs as the agent's account (no keys, no sudo). It holds the Slack
  connection (Socket Mode), answers only @-mentions in the agent's channel (and approvers' private messages),
  enforces the usage limits, and asks Claude, whose only way to run a command is the runner.

The runner needs only Python's standard library; the bot runs from its own uv environment with slack_bolt and
claude_agent_sdk, imported only by the bot.
"""

